---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import CtaBand from "../components/CtaBand.astro";
import { steps } from "../data/steps";

const description =
  "See how Straight Up Digital reviews your online presence, shares a clear report and helps you act on the most important next steps.";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How it works"
  description={description}
  canonicalPath="/how-it-works"
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container page-hero__inner">
      <div>
        <p class="kicker">How it works</p>
        <h1 class="page-hero__title">
          From a vague worry to a written plan.
        </h1>
        <div class="page-hero__actions">
          <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/digital-audit#request">
            Request your digital audit
            <svg class="btn__arrow" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 12h15M13 6l6 6-6 6"></path></svg>
          </a>
         </div>
      </div>
      <p class="page-hero__lede">
        Six steps, each with a clear job for you and a clear job for us. No
        retainer you did not ask for, and no work that starts before the scope is
        agreed.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="journey-title">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div>
          <p class="kicker"><span>01</span> The journey</p>
          <h2 class="h2" id="journey-title" style="margin-top: 14px;">
            What happens, in order.
          </h2>
        </div>
        <p class="lede">
          The first two steps are mostly ours. The third and fourth give you
          something concrete to decide on. The last two only happen if they earn
          their place.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="journey">
        {
          steps.map((step) => (
            <article class="journey__step">
              <div class="journey__num">{step.number}</div>
              <div class="journey__body">
                <h3 class="journey__title">{step.title}</h3>
                <div class="journey__cols">
                  <div class="journey__col">
                    <h4>You</h4>
                    <p>{step.client}</p>
                  </div>
                  <div class="journey__col">
                    <h4>We</h4>
                    <p>{step.we}</p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </article>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="need-title">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div>
          <p class="kicker"><span>02</span> Before we start</p>
          <h2 class="h2" id="need-title" style="margin-top: 14px;">
            What we need from you.
          </h2>
        </div>
        <p class="lede">
          Less than you would expect. The audit works from public information, so
          there is no long questionnaire and no access to your accounts for the
          first pass.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="factor-grid">
        <article class="factor">
          <h3>The website address</h3>
          <p>
            A domain is enough. If there is no website yet, say so. That becomes
            part of the finding rather than a reason to wait.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="factor">
          <h3>The business name and location</h3>
          <p>
            The name as customers see it, and the town or area the business
            actually serves. This is what we use to match listings and profiles.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="factor">
          <h3>What is not working</h3>
          <p>
            A sentence is enough. Few enquiries, wrong enquiries, an outdated
            site, no-shows from Maps. The symptom usually points to the category
            worth reading first.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="factor">
          <h3>Access, only when needed</h3>
          <p>
            For implementation work we may need access to a website, hosting or a
            business profile. We ask for the narrowest access that does the job,
            and never before the scope is agreed.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="limits-title">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div>
          <p class="kicker"><span>03</span> The honest part</p>
          <h2 class="h2" id="limits-title" style="margin-top: 14px; max-width: 16ch;">
            What this process cannot do.
          </h2>
        </div>
        <p class="lede">
          It cannot see your bank account, your analytics or your competitors'
          private data. It cannot promise a position in search results. It can
          show what is publicly visible and what to do about it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="limits">
        <ul>
          <li>
            It does not measure traffic, search volume, revenue or conversions.
          </li>
          <li>
            It does not guarantee rankings, enquiries or sales. Search results
            change for reasons outside anyone's control.
          </li>
          <li>
            It reflects public information at the time of the audit. A profile
            can change the day after the report is written.
          </li>
          <li>
            It is not a substitute for legal, financial or accounting advice.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <p class="body" style="margin-top: 28px;">
        Sending an enquiry is free. Any paid work is confirmed in writing before
        it starts, with the scope, the cost and the timing in one place.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand
    title="Ready to see what is actually there?"
    body="Send the website address and a sentence about what is not working. We will take it from there."
    secondaryLabel="What the audit checks"
    secondaryHref="/digital-audit#what-we-check"
  />
</BaseLayout>
